  "title": "Fail-closed pre-push review with a round budget",
  "summary": "The pre-push review stops being advisory. `--warn-only` is removed, so `osf review run` now exits non-zero on a kept must-fix or should-fix finding and on a review that could not run; a new round budget in the journal state lets a push through after three failed rounds, while a could-not-run streak ends blocked with a message. A credential preflight decides a missing key or login before any reviewer process starts, osf's own `.osf/` output is filtered out of the changed-file set so a round cannot change the next round's lens selection, and opencode's credential moves from `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` to its own `OPENCODE_API_KEY` (CI secret `OSF_REVIEW_OPENCODE_API_KEY`).",
